# Every text file is checked out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says (Git for
# Windows defaults it to true). check.sh and setup.sh compare config.kdl,
# plugins.sha256 and the docs line by line, and a CR at each line end breaks
# those comparisons, as it does a #!/bin/sh script; zellij and Windows editors
# read LF fine. The exception is zj.cmd: cmd.exe can misread labels and `goto`
# in a batch file with LF-only line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.wasm  binary
# Preserve exact upstream license text, including its final blank line.
licenses/*.txt whitespace=-blank-at-eof
